Qwen3-VL configuration/tokenizer assets are included for local tokenization.
Source: https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3-VL-8B-Instruct
Upstream lists Apache-2.0; the license text is included in LICENSE.
Their upstream notices continue to apply. Transformers, PyTorch,
Forge, bitsandbytes and attention/quantization kernels are external dependencies,
not relicensed or bundled by this extension.

Acceleration concepts were reviewed against Comfy-WaveSpeed (First Block Cache)
and ComfyUI Spectrum implementations. The added First Block Cache bridge is an
independent engine-local implementation; no ComfyUI node code is imported.

Modified inference files include pipeline.py and modeling_ideogram4.py:
compact text-feature capture, unconditional fast path, scoped acceleration,
host attention delegation, loading/lifecycle safeguards and block streaming.
See CHANGELOG.md.

No model weights, adapters, API credentials or personal config are distributed.
Those assets retain their separate licenses; Apache-2.0 here covers code only.
